WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.947
CTEs and windows are most useful when combined into a pipeline.

00:00:04.947 --> 00:00:10.137
The first CTE aggregates revenue to department-product grain.

00:00:10.137 --> 00:00:14.812
The second stage ranks those product totals inside each department.

00:00:14.812 --> 00:00:18.397
The final query filters to the top ranks.

00:00:18.397 --> 00:00:22.502
Each stage has a different job and a clear row meaning.

00:00:22.502 --> 00:00:29.552
A CTE gives a name to an intermediate result so a complex query can be read in stages.

00:00:29.552 --> 00:00:37.512
Use it to clarify grain changes and major transformations, not simply to break every two lines into a new

00:00:37.512 --> 00:00:44.942
block. A useful CTE name describes what the rows represent, such as patient_totals or ranked_visits.
